what's up guys i'm david from gamespot  and if you're a battlefield fan like me  particularly a battlefield 3 fan you may  have heard about the new reality mod  made by venice unleashed now this build  is incredibly rough around the edges and  it's really punishing if you don't know  what you're doing but there's also  something kind of infectious especially  if you have a proper squad i'm gonna  break down what makes the gameplay just  so quote realistic in this mod and how  it all works drop that like button sub  to the channel especially if you're  excited for future call of duty or  battlefield updates and let's get  started this mod was countless years in  the making by some very passionate and  dedicated people and i've been deep in  the trenches trying to figure out how  this gameplay lube actually works  fans of classic battlefield call of duty  games check your expectations at the  door i'm serious you might feel more at  home here if you come from arma squad or  tarkov so let's talk gameplay you will  live or die by your squad's teamwork and  team composition i am not kidding if you  don't have a mic get one right now or be  prepared to be extra attentive to the  squad team and general chats you will  need to communicate or be listening at  all times for call outs since it's  honestly kind of hard to tell what is  going on by yourself unless you're  leading the vanguard there is an  incredibly minimalist hud that only  shows your stamina a compass how many  mags your gun has which again mags not  rounds and what the fire rate of your  weapon is set to your kit is completely  restricted to the role that you want and  there are plenty of different roles but  not a lot of weapons there are rules for  machine gunners though breachers light  anti-tank medics riflemen and more each  role has a set weapon with specific  attachments and minimal scopes no  one-man armies players are significantly  slower in the reality mod than in the  original battlefield 3. this is  deliberate to prevent excessive solo  flanks or lone wolf type gameplay you're  with your team for the long haul and  your roles are meant to support each  other one thing that stands out from the  roles is a section for a specific squad  leader the squad leader has certain  abilities that they can do like marking  objectives and giving out orders to  their squads while also establishing  fobs or fobs which are basically remote  spawn points to help ease the pain of  dying and responding since by default  you have to spawn all the way at the end  of the map at your team's starting point  it's a journey you can't spawn on your  squad mates if you die and you can't  spawn on captured objective points fobs  are clutch and once established loki  kinda need an extra eye on them since  they can be destroyed by the enemy team  if you need another point midway and the  fob's a little bit too far away from  where you'd like to spawn you can put a  rally point down if you have enough  squad members near you and you're not  being rushed by the enemy team now so  far there was only the aas game mode  which is short for advanced and secure  no team death match no conquest no  domination no any of those game modes  you are used to from the og games from  what i've played aas is basically the  core rules of conquest aka you can  capture and hold objectives and both  teams have a set of tickets that go down  with each successive kill however  the pacing completely different the map  sizes are similar to a classic conquest  map and yet there are hardly any  vehicles with a few exceptions maps like  the gulf of oman have helicopters and  boats with an aircraft carrier spawn for  the american team but beyond that  traversal is incredibly slow putting  more emphasis on your squad leader  establishing tactical fobs another  significant change is the way that you  communicate with your team battlefield  and cod have various text chats letting  you type to your squad or team or you  know let off some steam in the general  chat which is a nice way of saying talk  [ __ ] after you get killed but the  reality mod takes things a step further  in how it implements the voice chat  you've got three different keybinds for  voice chats each indicated with a  different color representing who can  hear you green is for your squad and  only your squad no matter the distance  yeah get over here on my way sir  squad members on the other side of the  map can still hear you when you hop into  this channel blue though is a new  proximity chat letting you speak to  anyone on your team even if they aren't  in your squad so long they're within a  certain distance  [Applause]  you got him  yeah good kill in my experience the prox  chat has a pretty good range and was the  one that i relied on the most definitely  put some headphones on and enjoy because  they're spatial audio too however it you  know took me a minute to get used to but  i will say this proc chat came in clutch  when i was trying to find a down  teammate or asking for help on revives  on several occasions  appreciate it  lastly you have a red chat which is the  hq chat now from what i could tell that  privilege is restricted to the squad  leaders letting them figure out top  level tactical strategies on which  objectives to hold which to advance on  what the priority should be for their  squads and even things like calling in  artillery make sure we set up some fobs  over  gotcha yeah we're on it now if you're a  generally casual fps player all of this  might seem a bit too extreme and it is  especially at first but the trick is you  just have to remove your shyness and  embrace the role playing a bit seriously  everyone is going for the same objective  and they all want to have a good time so  don't be afraid  down the road  what a cheater  bridge right reach right now i disliked  the mod the most whenever i was rolling  my eyes on my teammates yelling contact  northwest and mark h06 k4 but i'm gonna  be real they had the right idea cause  see while i was being cynical and  judging them for embracing the  role-playing too much you know what my  reward was yeah dying almost immediately  fast forward a few days later in my  playtime and now i'm out there yelling  into the prox mic that i'm a medic ready  to assist my teammate's size of relief  and constant things felt to be honest  really good  okay  trust me if you want to have fun in this  mod let loose embrace the roll the more  that you go full send into the team  effort the more rewarding the gameplay  experience a thing to be cautious of is  if getting kills is what brings you the  most joy in these shooter games you  might have to tweak your expectations  just a little bit getting kills in the  reality mod is not necessarily difficult  but it's not easy either and i'm gonna  be real i am not unfamiliar to the 10  kill plus streaks in games like cod or  destiny but in this reality mod there  were no markers to indicate enemies they  blend in with their environment and the  weapons are kind of really inaccurate  especially in full auto mode there is no  way to heal yourself if you get hurt  unless you are near a medic and if you  get shot the most that you can do is  stop the bleeding with some field  dressing now you can use a health back  to heal yourself if you are a medic  however i ran into instances where i  eventually couldn't heal anymore not  sure if that was a bug or if you  eventually just run out so keep that in  mind just the warning i don't think that  getting the most kills is what will lead  your team to success although i  definitely had some folks on my teams  that were just going balls to the wall  getting kills left and right and i  appreciate them however i'm gonna say  this a smart machine gunner laying down  suppressing fire might be the person  that saves your life from enemy fire  rather than the cracked out twitch  streamer that normally racks up 40 plus  elims a game in a regular cod match  therefore it kind of makes sense that  most of the joy i got from this mod did  not come from trying to get kills but  rather embracing different roles being a  medic in particular felt the most  substantial you will notice there are a  lot of friendly fire instances  medics are constantly in demand some of  my favorite moments involved me  sprinting through the fire finding cover  behind rubble or smoke where a down  teammate was and bringing them back into  the fight i didn't spend as much time in  some of these other roles but i  appreciated their benefits when my  teammates were stepping up to the plate  many under the hood changes to the  gameplay distinguish this reality mod  from its battlefield 3 counterparts if  you see a game mode in the servers that  say aas alternative it is the same map  except at night a neat twist showcasing  the reality mods dynamic day night  system although fair warning if you are  playing a night map prepare to shield  your eyes because the transition today  is uh  a little sudden  [Music]  i just got blinded  now the reality mod is available now and  it does require you to own a genuine  copy of battlefield 3 alongside all of  its expansions on origin or ea however i  believe steam owners can still  technically make the mod work you'd have  to look it up but i'm pretty sure you  can direct the game file path into the  origin client and you'll be good to go  when you connect the two accounts to the  venice unleashed account now listen i  said earlier that this mod is not for  everyone to be honest it wasn't even for  me in the beginning i went through a lot  of frustration trying to figure the game  mode out i was particularly agitated  when dealing with less cooperative squad  mates or running into the game several  bugs and glitches however once the bumpy  initial rounds were kind of in the rear  view mirror i started finding roles that  i could appreciate like the medic and i  ended up enjoying some really fun  moments if there are some neat gameplay  mechanics i forgot to mention that you  enjoyed in this mod please feel free hop  into the comments again this is a mode  for players ready to go all in the role  playing a little bit and you know maybe  you have some experience in games like  squad or tarkov which never hurts that  being said if you've never played these  games give this mod a shot and who knows  you might just enjoy it  [Music]  [Music]

